a, Central","OECD"],"name":"INFOTEC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Edgar","key":"chavezpau","last":"Chavez","name":"Chavez, Edgar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eric S.","key":"tellezpau","last":"Tellez","name":"Tellez, Eric S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Similarity Search and Applications, SISAP 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d71616e7-7500-4871-9598-495ab85000e8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Overview of the SISAP 2023 Indexing Challenge","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712557","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Despite the broad range of algorithms for Approximate Nearest Neighbor Search, most empirical evaluations of algorithms have focused on smaller datasets, typically of 1 million points \\citep{Benchmark}. However, deploying recent advances in embedding based techniques for search, recommendation and ranking at scale require ANNS indices at billion, trillion or larger scale. Barring a few recent papers, there is limited consensus on which algorithms are effective at this scale vis-à-vis their hardware cost. This competition\\footnote{\\url{https://big-ann-benchmarks.com}} compares ANNS algorithms at billion-scale by hardware cost, accuracy and performance. We set up an open source evaluation framework\\footnote{\\url{https://github.com/harsha-simhadri/big-ann-benchmarks/}}% and leaderboards for both standardized and specialized hardware. The competition involves three tracks. The standard hardware track T1 evaluates algorithms on an Azure VM with limited DRAM, often the bottleneck in serving billion-scale indices, where the embedding data can be hundreds of GigaBytes in size. It uses FAISS \\citep{Faiss17} as the baseline. The standard hardware track T2 additional allows inexpensive SSDs in addition to the limited DRAM and uses DiskANN \\citep{DiskANN19} as the baseline. The specialized hardware track T3 allows any hardware configuration, and again uses FAISS as the baseline. We compiled six diverse billion-scale datasets, four newly released for this competition, that span a variety of modalities, data types, dimensions, deep learning models, distance functions and sources. The outcome of the competition was ranked leaderboards of algorithms in each track based on recall at a query throughput threshold. Additionally, for track T3, separate leaderboards were created based on recall as well as cost-normalized and power-normalized query throughput.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Simhadri, Hasha","Williams, George","Douze, Matthijs","Babenko, Artem","Baranchuk, Dmitry","Hosseini, Lucas","Krishnaswamny, Ravishankar","Srinivasa, Gopal","Subramanya, Suhas Jayaram","Wang, Jingdong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384427"],"event":{"acronym":"NeurIPS","title":"Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Russia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baidu","Carnegie Mellon University","GSI Technology","Meta AI","Microsoft Research","Yandex"],"keyword":["Approximate Nearest Neighbor Search","Billion Scale Dataset","Deep Learning Models","Evaluation framework","Hardware Cost"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"results of the neurips 000000000021 challenge on billion scale approximate nearest neighbor search","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v176/simhadri22a.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384427","identifier":[{"id":"85147383313","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d6c12c8d-7ee3-459b-8c68-1e2b2c124677"],"keyword":["Approximate Nearest Neighbor Search","Billion-Scale Dataset","Deep Learning Models","Evaluation Framework","Hardware Cost"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AE554A99A4E568C489E228C40DDD5681"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v176/simhadri22a.html","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"microsoft research","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Microsoft Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"gsi technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"GSI Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"meta ai","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Meta AI","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ru","key":"yandex","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Yandex","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"carnegie mellon university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Mellon University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"baidu","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Baidu","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasha","key":"simhadripau","last":"Simhadri","name":"Simhadri, Hasha","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"George","key":"williamspau","last":"Williams","name":"Williams, George","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthijs","key":"douzepau","last":"Douze","name":"Douze, Matthijs","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Artem","key":"babenkopau","last":"Babenko","name":"Babenko, Artem","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Dmitry","key":"baranchukpau","last":"Baranchuk","name":"Baranchuk, Dmitry","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucas","key":"hosseinipau","last":"Hosseini","name":"Hosseini, Lucas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ravishankar","key":"krishnaswamnypau","last":"Krishnaswamny","name":"Krishnaswamny, Ravishankar","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gopal","key":"srinivasapau","last":"Srinivasa","name":"Srinivasa, Gopal","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Suhas Jayaram","key":"subramanyapau","last":"Subramanya","name":"Subramanya, Suhas Jayaram","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingdong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jingdong","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"177-189","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the NeurIPS 2021 Competitions and Demonstrations Track","volume":"176"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d6c12c8d-7ee3-459b-8c68-1e2b2c124677"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Results of the NeurIPS’21 Challenge on Billion-Scale Approximate Nearest Neighbor Search","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384427","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Representing a sparse histogram, or more generally a sparse vector, is a fundamental task in differential privacy. An ideal solution would require space close to information-theoretical lower bounds, have an error distribution that depends optimally on the desired privacy level, and allow fast random access to entries in the vector. However, existing approaches have only achieved two of these three goals. In this paper we introduce the Approximate Laplace Projection (ALP) mechanism for approximating k-sparse vectors. This mechanism is shown to simultaneously have information-theoretically optimal space (up to constant factors), fast access to vector entries, and error of the same magnitude as the Laplace mechanism applied to dense vectors. A key new technique is a unary representation of small integers, which we show to be robust against “randomized response” noise. This representation is combined with hashing, in the spirit of Bloom filters, to obtain a space-efficient, differentially private representation. Our theoretical performance bounds are complemented by simulations showing that the constant factors on the main performance parameters are quite small and supporting practicality of the technique.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Lebeda, Christian Janos","Pagh, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S02-089.89-038322"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Algorithms","Differential Privacy","Histograms","Sparse Vectors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"representing sparse vectors with differential privacy low error optimal space and fast access","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.29012/jpc.809","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.89-038322","identifier":[{"id":"85140973339","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-712c9f90-b7b3-4ca3-91ed-b67ac1ed9a45","ku-7118a4f7-935b-4c79-b1f8-a68803a409cf"],"keyword":["Algorithms","differential privacy","histograms","sparse vectors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8A9CB019711568957B62E51932386F70"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/340691565/REPRESENTING_SPARSE.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.29012/jpc.809","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Janos","key":"lebedapau","last":"Lebeda","locid":"a0e31b8c-3d9c-4b68-834d-d4c06914b69f","name":"Lebeda, Christian Janos","orcid":"0000-0001-9517-8466","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","locid":"044bf2b8-4ea6-4c2e-984c-88a0267151c7","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-1516-9306","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.29012/jpc.809","issn":["25758527"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Privacy and Confidentiality","status":"p","title":"Journal of Privacy and Confidentiality","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140973339"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-712c9f90-b7b3-4ca3-91ed-b67ac1ed9a45","ku-7118a4f7-935b-4c79-b1f8-a68803a409cf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Representing Sparse Vectors with Differential Privacy, Low Error, Optimal Space, and Fast Access","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.89-038322","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Similarity search is a fundamental algorithmic primitive, widely used in many computer science disciplines. Given a set of points S and a radius parameter r > 0, the r-near neighbor (r-NN) problem asks for a data structure that, given any query point q, returns a point p within distance at most r from q. In this paper, we study the r-NN problem in the light of individual fairness and providing equal opportunities: all points that are within distance r from the query should have the same probability to be returned. In the low-dimensional case, this problem was first studied by Hu, Qiao, and Tao (PODS 2014). Locality sensitive hashing (LSH), the theoretically strongest approach to similarity search in high dimensions, does not provide such a fairness guarantee.In this work, we show that LSH based algorithms can be made fair, without a significant loss in efficiency. We propose several efficient data structures for the exact and approximate variants of the fair NN problem. Our approach works more generally for sampling uniformly from a sub-collection of sets of a given collection and can be used in a few other applications. We also develop a data structure for fair similarity search under inner product that requires nearly-linear space and exploits locality sensitive filters. The paper concludes with an experimental evaluation that highlights the unfairness of state-of-the-art NN data structures and shows the performance of our algorithms on real-world datasets.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Har-Peled, Sariel","Mahabadi, Sepideh","Pagh, Rasmus","Silvestri, Francesco"],"cuid":["S02-090.47-038411"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of Padua"],"keyword":["Fairness","Locality sensitive hashing","Near Neighbor","Sampling","Similarity search"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sampling a near neighbor in high dimensions who is the fairest of them all","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502867","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.47-038411","identifier":[{"id":"85129852069","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f58e4759-09e5-413f-a7ac-378039ff9626","ku-3d721e0c-f23c-4b31-a63d-ebfd6c4ff2df"],"keyword":["Similarity search","fairness","locality sensitive hashing","near neighbor","sampling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F7FD607F136C0383604E15317DDC24A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357047734/Sampling_a_Near_Neighbor_in_High_Dimensions.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502867","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92939802/Fair_Nearest_Neighbor_TODS_author.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of illinois at urbana champaign","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"toyota technological institute at chicago","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"university of padua","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padua","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sariel","key":"harpeledpau","last":"Har-Peled","name":"Har-Peled, Sariel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sepideh","key":"mahabadipau","last":"Mahabadi","name":"Mahabadi, Sepideh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","locid":"044bf2b8-4ea6-4c2e-984c-88a0267151c7","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-1516-9306","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Francesco","key":"silvestripau","last":"Silvestri","name":"Silvestri, Francesco","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3502867","issn":["03625915","15574644"],"issn_org":["03625915"],"issue":"1","journal":"ACM Transactions on Database Systems","pages":"1-40","paperid":"4","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Database Systems","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129852069"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f58e4759-09e5-413f-a7ac-378039ff9626","ku-3d721e0c-f23c-4b31-a63d-ebfd6c4ff2df"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sampling a Near Neighbor in High Dimensions-Who is the Fairest of Them All?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.47-038411","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Similarity search is a fundamental algorithmic primitive, widely used in many computer science disciplines. Given a set of points S and a radius parameter r > 0, the r-near neighbor (r-NN) problem asks for a data structure that, given any query point q, returns a point p within distance at most r from q. In this paper, we study the r-NN problem in the light of individual fairness and providing equal opportunities: all points that are within distance r from the query should have the same probability to be returned. The problem is of special interest in high dimensions, where Locality Sensitive Hashing (LSH), the theoretically leading approach to similarity search, does not provide any fairness guarantee. In this work, we show that LSH-based algorithms can be made fair, without a significant loss in efficiency. We propose several efficient data structures for the exact and approximate variants of the fair NN problem. Our approach works more generally for sampling uniformly from a sub-collection of sets of a given collection and can be used in a few other applications. We also carried out an experimental evaluation that highlights the inherent unfairness of existing NN data structures.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Har-Peled, Sariel","Mahabadi, Sepideh","Pagh, Rasmus","Silvestri, Francesco"],"cuid":["S02-092.73-038391"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago","University of Illinois","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of Padova","University of Padua"],"keyword":["High dimensional data structures","Individual fairness","Locality sensitive hashing","Similarity search","r near neighbor problem"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sampling near neighbors in search for fairness","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357080615/Sampling_Near_Neighbors_in_Search_for_Fairness.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-092.73-038391","identifier":[{"id":"85135707549","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d90d723a-ad7a-414f-9704-ed3b9a01c86f","ku-87ad12e8-6914-4579-8d1d-e017f8f7d161"],"keyword":["Locality Sensitive Hashing","Similarity search","high-dimensional data structures","individual fairness","r-near neighbor problem"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0DFF90878AA5013FE90D9875E62EA08B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357080615/Sampling_Near_Neighbors_in_Search_for_Fairness.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93078038/Fair_Nearest_Neighbor_TODS_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of illinois at urbana champaign","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of illinois","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"toyota technological institute at chicago","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"it","key":"university of padua","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padua","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"it","key":"university of padova","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padova","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Sariel","key":"harpeledpau","last":"Har-Peled","name":"Har-Peled, Sariel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Sepideh","key":"mahabadipau","last":"Mahabadi","name":"Mahabadi, Sepideh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 1","first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","locid":"044bf2b8-4ea6-4c2e-984c-88a0267151c7","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-1516-9306","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","first":"Francesco","key":"silvestripau","last":"Silvestri","name":"Silvestri, Francesco","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3543667","issn":["00010782","10591192"],"issn_org":["00010782"],"issue":"8","journal":"Communications of the ACM","pages":"83-90","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Communications of the ACM","title_org":"Communications of the A C M","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135707549"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d90d723a-ad7a-414f-9704-ed3b9a01c86f","ku-87ad12e8-6914-4579-8d1d-e017f8f7d161"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sampling near neighbors in search for fairness","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.73-038391","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Kernel Density Estimation (KDE) is a nonparametric method for estimatig the shape of a density function, given a set of samples from the distribution. Recently, locality-sensitive hashing, originally proposed as a tool for nearest neighbor search, has been shown to enable fast KDE data structures. However, these approaches do not take advantage of the many other advances that have been made in algorithms for nearest neighbor algorithms. We present an algorithm called Density Estimation from Approximate Nearest Neighbors (DEANN) where we apply Approximate Nearest Neighbor (ANN) algorithms as a black box subroutine to compute an unbiased KDE. The idea is to find points that have a large contribution to the KDE using ANN, compute their contribution exactly, and approximate the remainder with Random Sampling (RS). We present a theoretical argument that supports the idea that an ANN subroutine can speed up the evaluation. Furthermore, we provide a C++ implementation with a Python interface that can make use of an arbitrary ANN implementation as a subroutine for KDE evaluation. We show empirically that our implementation outperforms state of the art implementations in all high dimensional datasets we considered, and matches the performance of RS in cases where the ANN yield no gains in performance.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Karppa, Matti","Aumüller, Martin","Pagh, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-522260"],"event":{"end":"2022-03-30","place":"Virtuel, unknown","start":"2022-03-28","title":"25th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS)","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deann speeding up kernel density estimation using approximate nearest neighbor search","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/340695310/DEANN.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-522260","ids":["ku-d7a0e5c0-b1b0-4a09-803b-2c81c6b519ad"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-C5C502F45729DA1240FB90D3C84BC878"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/340695310/DEANN.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v151/karppa22a.html","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Matti","key":"karppapau","last":"Karppa","name":"Karppa, Matti","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","name":"Aumüller, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","locid":"044bf2b8-4ea6-4c2e-984c-88a0267151c7","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-1516-9306","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26403498"],"pages":"3108-3137","publisher":"PMLR","series":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 25th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144263137"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d7a0e5c0-b1b0-4a09-803b-2c81c6b519ad"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DEANN : Speeding up Kernel-Density Estimation using Approximate Nearest Neighbor Search","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-522260","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT Similarity joins are a basic primitive in data mining. Given two sets of points, we are interested in reporting all pairs of points whose similarity is above a user-defined threshold. Solving the problem naively entails verifying all possible pairs, which can be infeasible for large inputs. In such contexts, Locality Sensitive Hashing (LSH) is often considered to reduce the number of pairs to verify. However, while it provides subquadratic running time, large input sets make it nevertheless necessary to resort to distributed computing. Hu, Yi, and Tao (PODS’17, TODS’19) proposed a nearly load-optimal LSH-based join algorithm and provided a small-scale experimental study in a distributed setting. This paper provides further analysis of their approach. It shows that the load-minimizing parameter settings by Hu et al. incur too much local work, rendering it impractical. To remedy this drawback, we propose two approaches: The first distributes work in a data-independent way, while the second adapts to the data distribution using LSH. Both schemes then use LSH to solve subproblems locally. This allows to balance load and the amount of local work. Through an experimental evaluation, we show that the transition from theory to practice for Hu et al.’s approach is challenging: it is hard to strike a good tradeoff between the load and the amount of local work of each processor, load balancing is itself an issue, and LSH may introduce duplicates in the output. Our extensive experimental evaluation is supported by an efficient open source implementation of all the methods we test. Our results highlight the need for an holistic approach: only focusing on the load, as tradition in the MPC model, might not make efficient use the available resources and better trade-offs between local work and load are possible.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Ceccarello, Matteo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384139"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data Mining methods","Distributed computing","Load balancing","Locality Sensitive Hashing LSH","Similarity Joins"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implementing distributed approximate similarity joins using locality sensitive hashing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5441/002/edbt.2022.07","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384139","identifier":[{"id":"85127299281","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c3cfa9b9-6ea4-45db-9111-e9374b49571a"],"keyword":["Data Mining Methods","Distributed Computing","Load Balancing","Locality Sensitive Hashing (LSH)","Similarity Joins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A1579CA0E844EDFCB2232532A17B0EFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5441/002/edbt.2022.07","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"ceccarellopau","last":"Ceccarello","name