{"abstract":"We revisit our contributions on visual sentiment analysis for online review images published at ACM Multimedia 2017, where we develop item-oriented and user-oriented convolutional neural networks that better capture the interaction of image features with specific expressions of users or items. In this work, we outline the experimental claims as well as describe the procedures to reproduce the results therein. In addition, we provide artifacts including data sets and code to replicate the experiments.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Truong, Quoc-Tuan","Lauw, Hady W","Aumüller, Martin","Nitta, Naoko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382011"],"event":{"acronym":"MM","title":"ACM Multimedia"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South","OECD"],"country":["Japan","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Osaka Medical and Pharmaceutical University","Singapore Management University"],"keyword":["Convolutional neural networks","Data Sets and Code","Experimental Reproducibility","Online Review Images","Visual Sentiment Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reproducibility companion paper visual sentiment analysis for review images with item oriented and user oriented cnn","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85564711/ACM_MM_2020_Repro_Paper29061.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382011","identifier":[{"id":"85106903862","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-330acc26-5c63-4760-8d2b-50b4fa5d2ee1"],"keyword":["Convolutional Neural Networks","Data Sets and Code","Experimental Reproducibility","Online Review Images","Visual Sentiment Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E553E8108B777D88484CCBF36C3C4800"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85564711/ACM_MM_2020_Repro_Paper29061.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"sg","key":"singapore management university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Singapore Management University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"osaka medical and pharmaceutical university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Osaka Medical and Pharmaceutical University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Quoc-Tuan","key":"truongpau","last":"Truong","name":"Truong, Quoc-Tuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hady W","key":"lauwpau","last":"Lauw","name":"Lauw, Hady W","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Naoko","key":"nittapau","last":"Nitta","name":"Nitta, Naoko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3394171.3414813","pages":"4444-4447","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"MM '20: Proceedings of the 28th ACM International Conference on Multimedia"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106903862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-330acc26-5c63-4760-8d2b-50b4fa5d2ee1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reproducibility Companion Paper: Visual Sentiment Analysis for Review Images with Item-Oriented and User-Oriented CNN","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382011","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Similarity search problems in high-dimensional data arise in many areas of computer science such as data bases, image analysis, machine learning, and natural language processing. One of the most prominent problems is finding the k nearest neighbors of a data point q 2 Rd in a large set of data points S Rd, under same distance measure such as Euclidean distance. In contrast to lower dimensional settings, we do not know of worst-case efficient data structures for such search problems in high-dimensional data, i.e., data structures that are faster than a linear scan through the data set. However, there is a rich body of (often heuristic) approaches that solve nearest neighbor search problems much faster than such a scan on many real-world data sets. As a necessity, the term solve means that these approaches give approximate results that are close to the true k-nearest neighbors. In this talk, we survey recent approaches to nearest neighbor search and related problems. The talk consists of three parts: (1) What makes nearest neighbor search difficult? (2) How do current state-of-the-art algorithms work? (3) What are recent advances regarding similarity search on GPUs, in distributed settings, or in external memory?","author_count":1,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382670"],"event":{"acronym":"sea","title":"International Symposium on Experimental Algorithms"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Approximate algorithms","Euclidean distance","High dimensional data","Nearest neighbor search","Similarity search"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"algorithm engineering for high dimensional similarity search problems invited talk","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SEA.2020.1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382670","identifier":[{"id":"85088167637","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5d9a349e-c59c-4405-aa16-7911c335284d"],"keyword":["Approximate algorithms","Euclidean distance","High-dimensional data","Nearest neighbor search","Similarity search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B4458C4A2F220A0D382903FD4AAAEE84"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SEA.2020.1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506485/LIPIcs_SEA_2020_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.sea.2020.1","issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"18th International Symposium on Experimental Algorithms (SEA 2020)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088167637"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5d9a349e-c59c-4405-aa16-7911c335284d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Algorithm Engineering for High-Dimensional Similarity Search Problems (Invited Talk)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382670","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Similarity search is a fundamental algorithmic primitive, widely used in many computer science disciplines. There are several variants of the similarity search problem, and one of the most relevant is the r-near neighbor (r-NN) problem: given a radius r>0 and a set of points S, construct a data structure that, for any given query point q, returns a point p within distance at most r from q. In this paper, we study the r-NN problem in the light of fairness. We consider fairness in the sense of equal opportunity: all points that are within distance r from the query should have the same probability to be returned. In the low-dimensional case, this problem was first studied by Hu, Qiao, and Tao (PODS 2014). Locality sensitive hashing (LSH), the theoretically strongest approach to similarity search in high dimensions, does not provide such a fairness guarantee. To address this, we propose efficient data structures for r-NN where all points in S that are near q have the same probability to be selected and returned by the query. Specifically, we first propose a black-box approach that, given any LSH scheme, constructs a data structure for uniformly sampling points in the neighborhood of a query. Then, we develop a data structure for fair similarity search under inner product that requires nearly-linear space and exploits locality sensitive filters. The paper concludes with an experimental evaluation that highlights (un)fairness in a recommendation setting on real-world datasets and discusses the inherent unfairness introduced by solving other variants of the problem.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Pagh, Rasmus","Silvestri, Francesco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383942"],"event":{"acronym":"PODS","title":"ACM SIGMOD-SIGACT-SIGAI Symposium on Principles of Database Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fairness","Locality sensitive hashing","Similarity search","Uniform Sampling","r Near Neighbor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fair near neighbor search independent range sampling in high dimensions pods","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506339/1906.01859.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383942","identifier":[{"id":"85086224769","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b7839de0-0ab0-4683-adc9-7ef088229d27"],"keyword":["Fairness","Locality Sensitive Hashing","Similarity Search","Uniform Sampling","r-Near Neighbor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5BAA4D9B4DE8B1341D6EB98804792978"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506339/1906.01859.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesco","key":"silvestripau","last":"Silvestri","name":"Silvestri, Francesco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3375395.3387648","pages":"191-204","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"PODS'20: Proceedings of the 39th ACM SIGMOD-SIGACT-SIGAI Symposium on Principles of Database Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086224769"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b7839de0-0ab0-4683-adc9-7ef088229d27"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fair Near Neighbor Search: Independent Range Sampling in High Dimensions. PODS","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383942","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes two locally-differential private algorithms for releasing user vectors such that the Jaccard similarity between these vectors can be efficiently estimated. The basic building block is the well known MinHash method. To achieve a privacy-utility trade-off, MinHash is extended in two ways using variants of Generalized Randomized Response and the Laplace Mechanism. A theoretical analysis provides bounds on the absolute error and experiments show the utility-privacy trade-off on synthetic and real-world data. A full version of this paper is available at http://arxiv.org/abs/2008.08134.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Bourgeat, no-firstname","Schmurr, no-firstname"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384599"],"event":{"acronym":"SISAP","title":"International Conference on Similarity Search and Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Generalized Randomized Response","Jaccard Similarity","Laplace Mechanism","Locally Differential Privacy","MinHash"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differentially private sketches for jaccard similarity estimation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506373/2008.08134.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384599","identifier":[{"id":"85093838643","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e2040632-f8d3-4a77-9c92-2aa37204aab7"],"keyword":["Generalized Randomized Response","Jaccard Similarity","Laplace Mechanism","Locally Differential Privacy","MinHash"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD8961C432125361EB3AD4C09D71E33F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506373/2008.08134.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"no-firstname","key":"bourgeatpau","last":"Bourgeat","name":"Bourgeat, no-firstname","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"no-firstname","key":"schmurrpau","last":"Schmurr","name":"Schmurr, no-firstname","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-60936-8_2","issn":["03029743"],"pages":"18-32","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notest in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"SISAP 2020","title":"International Conference on Similarity Search and Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85093838643"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e2040632-f8d3-4a77-9c92-2aa37204aab7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Differentially Private Sketches for Jaccard Similarity Estimation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384599","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents simple variants of the BlockQuicksort algorithm described by Edelkamp and Weiss (ESA 2016). The simplification is achieved by using Lomuto's partitioning scheme instead of Hoare's crossing pointer technique to partition the input. To achieve a robust sorting algorithm that works well on many different input types, the paper introduces a novel two-pivot variant of Lomuto's partitioning scheme. A surprisingly simple twist to the generic two-pivot quicksort approach makes the algorithm robust. The paper provides an analysis of the theoretical properties of the proposed algorithms and compares them to their competitors. The analysis shows that Lomuto-based approaches incur a higher average sorting cost than the Hoare-based approach of BlockQuicksort. Moreover, the analysis is particularly useful to reason about pivot choices that suit the two-pivot approach. An extensive experimental study shows that, despite their worse theoretical behavior, the simpler variants perform as well as the original version of BlockQuicksort.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Hass, Nikolaj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383511"],"event":{"acronym":"ALENEX","title":"Workshop on Algorithm Engineering and Experiments"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["BlockQuicksort","Lomuto s partitioning scheme","Pivot selection strategies","Sorting algorithm analysis","Two pivot quicksort"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simple and fast blockquicksort using lomuto s partitioning scheme","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611975499.2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383511","identifier":[{"id":"85065201958","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-989f6501-78f9-4ce1-ad61-61baa00ece82"],"keyword":["BlockQuicksort","Lomuto's partitioning scheme","Pivot selection strategies","Sorting algorithm analysis","Two-pivot quicksort"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-EDC8150F4B141132A9015C4EB890262F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84710077/1810.12047.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611975499.2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolaj","key":"hasspau","last":"Hass","name":"Hass, Nikolaj","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611975499.2","eisbn":["9781611975499"],"publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"2019 Proceedings of the Twenty-First Workshop on Algorithm Engineering and Experiments (ALENEX)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-989f6501-78f9-4ce1-ad61-61baa00ece82"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Simple and Fast BlockQuicksort using Lomuto's Partitioning Scheme","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383511","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper reconsiders common benchmarking approaches to nearest neighbor search. It is shown that the concept of local intrinsic dimensionality (LID) allows to choose query sets of a wide range of difficulty for real-world datasets. Moreover, the effect of different LID distributions on the running time performance of implementations is empirically studied. To this end, different visualization concepts are introduced that allow to get a more fine-grained overview of the inner workings of nearest neighbor search principles. The paper closes with remarks about the diversity of datasets commonly used for nearest neighbor search benchmarking. It is shown that such real-world datasets are not diverse: results on a single dataset predict results on all other datasets well.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Ceccarello, Matteo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382261"],"event":{"acronym":"SISAP","title":"International Conference on Similarity Search and Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cs DB","cs IR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of local intrinsic dimensionality in benchmarking nearest neighbor search","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84731980/1907.07387.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382261","identifier":[{"id":"85076088872","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-42df4cfd-992e-45fa-89ba-2653904b149b"],"keyword":["cs.DB","cs.IR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-82693D9A767FC81EED4EA02E0458F207"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84731980/1907.07387.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.07387","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"ceccarellopau","last":"Ceccarello","name":"Ceccarello, Matteo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-32047-8_11","eisbn":["9783030320478"],"isbn":["9783030320461"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"SISAP 2019: Similarity Search and Applications","title":"International Conference on Similarity Search and Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076088872"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-42df4cfd-992e-45fa-89ba-2653904b149b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Role of Local Intrinsic Dimensionality in Benchmarking Nearest Neighbor Search","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382261","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper reconsiders common benchmarking approaches to nearest neighbor search. It is shown that the concept of local intrinsic dimensionality (LID) allows to choose query sets of a wide range of diculty for real-world datasets. Moreover, the eect of dierent LID distributions on the running time performance of implementations is empirically studied. To this end, dierent visualization concepts are introduced that allow to get a more ne-grained overview of the inner workings of nearest neighbor earch principles. The paper closes with remarks about the diversity of datasets commonly used for nearest neighbor search benchmarking. It is shown that such real-world datasets are not diverse: results on a single dataset predict results on all other datasets well.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Ceccarello, Matteo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382519"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmarking","Nearest neighbor search","Visualization","dataset diversity","local intrinsic dimensionality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"benchmarking nearest neighbor search influence of local intrinsic dimensionality and result diversity in real world datasets","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2436/article_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382519","identifier":[{"id":"85072750031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5357f8c6-75e6-4e58-9516-49392bbe1e34"],"keyword":["benchmarking","dataset diversity","local intrinsic dimensionality","nearest neighbor search","visualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-39C63D2886F2AD397B1B39154B728DA2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2436/article_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84710082/article_3.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"ceccarellopau","last":"Ceccarello","name":"Ceccarello, Matteo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"publisher":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","series":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"EDML 2019 - Evaluation and Experimental Design in Data Mining and Machine Learning","volume":"2436"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072750031"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5357f8c6-75e6-4e58-9516-49392bbe1e34"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Benchmarking Nearest Neighbor Search: Influence of Local Intrinsic Dimensionality and Result Diversity in Real-World Datasets","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382519","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes ANN-Benchmarks, a tool for evaluating the performance of in-memory approximate nearest neighbor algorithms. It provides a standard interface for measuring the performance and quality achieved by nearest neighbor algorithms on different standard data sets. It supports several different ways of integrating -NN algorithms, and its configuration system automatically tests a range of parameter settings for each algorithm. Algorithms are compared with respect to many different (approximate) quality measures, and adding more is easy and fast; the included plotting front-ends can visualize these as images, LaTeX plots, and websites with interactive plots. ANN-Benchmarks aims to provide a constantly updated overview of the current state of the art of -NN algorithms. In the short term, this overview allows users to choose the correct -NN algorithm and parameters for their similarity search task; in the longer term, algorithm designers will be able to use this overview to test and refine automatic parameter tuning. The paper gives an overview of the system, evaluates the results of the benchmark, and points out directions for future work. Interestingly, very different approaches to -NN search yield comparable quality-performance trade-offs. The system is available at http://ann-benchmarks.com.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Bernhardsson, Erik","Faithfull, Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382892"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmarking","Evaluation","Nearest neighbor search"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ann benchmarks a benchmarking tool for approximate nearest neighbor algorithms","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.05614","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382892","identifier":[{"id":"85062146075","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6cf67c5c-dfc0-417e-a18a-b97725dee504"],"keyword":["benchmarking","evaluation","nearest neighbor search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F83C3A8BABF1AF7EE323BC02A7522500"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84719223/1807.05614.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.05614","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"bernhardssonpau","last":"Bernhardsson","name":"Bernhardsson, Erik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"faithfullpau","last":"Faithfull","name":"Faithfull, Alexander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.is.2019.02.006","issn":["03064379","18736076"],"issn_org":["03064379"],"journal":"Information Systems","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Information Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062146075"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6cf67c5c-dfc0-417e-a18a-b97725dee504"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"ANN-Benchmarks: A benchmarking tool for approximate nearest neighbor algorithms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382892","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We present PUFFINN, a parameterless LSH-based index for solving the $k$-nearest neighbor problem with probabilistic guarantees. By parameterless we mean that the user is only required to specify the amount of memory the index is supposed to use and the result quality that should be achieved. The index combines several heuristic ideas known in the literature. By small adaptions to the query algorithm, we make heuristics rigorous. We perform experiments on real-world and synthetic inputs to evaluate implementation choices and show that the implementation satisfies the quality guarantees while being competitive with other state-of-the-art approaches to nearest neighbor search. We describe a novel synthetic data set that is difficult to solve for almost all existing nearest neighbor search approaches, and for which PUFFINN significantly outperform previous methods.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christiani, Tobias Lybecker","Pagh, Rasmus","Aumüller, Martin","Vesterli, Michael Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383035"],"event":{"acronym":"ESA","title":"European Symposium on Algorithms"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Heuristic algorithms","Locality sensitive hashing","Parameterless indexing","Probabilistic guarantees","k nearest neighbor search"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"puffinn parameterless and universally fast finding of nearest neighbors","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2019.10","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383035","identifier":[{"id":"85074852849","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-77b537dc-c78a-4073-b009-4a994f5ccbe0"],"keyword":["Heuristic algorithms","Locality-sensitive hashing","Parameterless indexing","Probabilistic guarantees","k-nearest neighbor search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-46684FB352E96AEF9D6F224C1ED7348C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2019.10","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84710087/LIPIcs_ESA_2019_10.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias Lybecker","key":"christianipau","last":"Christiani","name":"Christiani, Tobias Lybecker","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Erik","key":"vesterlipau","last":"Vesterli","name":"Vesterli, Michael Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.esa.2019.10","eisbn":["9783959771245"],"pages":"1-16","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"27th Annual European Symposium on Algorithms (ESA 2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074852849"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-77b537dc-c78a-4073-b009-4a994f5ccbe0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PUFFINN: Parameterless and Universally Fast FInding of Nearest Neighbors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383035","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We present an average-case analysis of a variant of dual-pivot quicksort. We show that the algorithmic partitioning strategy used is optimal, that is, it minimizes the expected number of key comparisons. For the analysis, we calculate the expected number of comparisons exactly as well as asymptotically; in particular, we provide exact expressions for the linear, logarithmic and constant terms. An essential step is the analysis of zeros of lattice paths in a certain probability model. Along the way a combinatorial identity is proved.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Dietzfelbinger, Martin","Heuberger, Clemens","Krenn, Daniel","Prodinger, Helmut"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381523"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","South Africa"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ilmenau University of Technology","Stellenbosch University","University of Klagenfurt"],"keyword":["Dual pivot quicksort","asymptotic enumeration","combinatorial identity","lattice paths"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dual pivot quicksort optimality analysis and zeros of associated lattice paths","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83279842/1611.00258.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381523","identifier":[{"id":"85052716915","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1136845c-ea3f-4076-8a99-9c86af3cc079"],"keyword":["Dual-pivot quicksort","asymptotic enumeration","combinatorial identity","lattice paths"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E2C1CE2C9DD29BD77CFBB04993829B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83279842/1611.00258.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ilmenau university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ilmenau University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"university of klagenfurt","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Klagenfurt","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"za","key":"stellenbosch university","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"Stellenbosch University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"dietzfelbingerpau","last":"Dietzfelbinger","name":"Dietzfelbinger, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Clemens","key":"heubergerpau","last":"Heuberger","name":"Heuberger, Clemens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"krennpau","last":"Krenn","name":"Krenn, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Helmut","key":"prodingerpau","last":"Prodinger","name":"Prodinger, Helmut","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s096354831800041x","issn":["09635483","14692163"],"issn_org":["09635483"],"journal":"Combinatorics, Probability & Computing","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Combinatorics, Probability & Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052716915"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1136845c-ea3f-4076-8a99-9c86af3cc079"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dual-Pivot Quicksort: Optimality, Analysis and Zeros of Associated Lattice Paths","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381523","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Locality-sensitive hashing (LSH) is an important tool for managing high-dimensional noisy or uncertain data, for example in connection with data cleaning (similarity join) and noise-robust search (similarity search). However, for a number of problems the LSH framework is not known to yield good solutions, and instead ad hoc solutions have been designed for particular similarity and distance measures. For example, this is true for output-sensitive similarity search/join, and for indexes supporting annulus queries that aim to report a point close to a certain given distance from the query point. In this paper we initiate the study of distance-sensitive hashing (DSH), a generalization of LSH that seeks a family of hash functions such that the probability of two points having the same hash value is a given function of the distance between them. More precisely, given a distance space (X, dist ) and a \"collision probability function\" (CPF) f: R -> [0,1] we seek a distribution over pairs of functions (h,g) such that for every pair of points x, y ın X the collision probability is Pr[h(x)=g(y)] = f(dist(x,y)). Locality-sensitive hashing is the study of how fast a CPF can decrease as the distance grows. For many spaces, f can be made exponentially decreasing even if we restrict attention to the symmetric case where g=h. We show that the asymmetry achieved by having a pair of functions makes it possible to achieve CPFs that are, for example, increasing or unimodal, and show how this leads to principled solutions to problems not addressed by the LSH framework. This includes a novel application to privacy-preserving distance estimation. We believe that the DSH framework will find further applications in high-dimensional data management. To put the running time bounds of the proposed constructions into perspective, we show lower bounds for the performance of DSH constructions with increasing and decreasing CPFs under angular distance. Essentially, this shows that our constructions are tight up to lower order terms. In particular, we extend existing LSH lower bounds, showing that they also hold in the asymmetric setting.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Christiani, Tobias","Pagh, Rasmus","Silvestri, Francesco"],"cuid":["S02-096.41-038407"],"event":{"acronym":"PODS","end":"2018-06-15","place":"Houston, us","start":"2018-06-10","title":"37th ACM SIGMOD-SIGACT-SIGAI Symposium on Principles of Database Systems","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Padova"],"keyword":["Collision Probability Function","Distance Sensitive Hashing","High Dimensional Data Management","Locality sensitive hashing","Privacy Preserving Distance Estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distance sensitive hashing","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83278586/1703.07867.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-096.41-038407","identifier":[{"id":"85048008546","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ea56a443-a602-4cc9-88d5-b3544dabeac1","ku-c7995700-8fe0-4e70-9a2d-ded719bd3815"],"keyword":["Collision Probability Function","Distance-Sensitive Hashing","High-Dimensional Data Management","Locality-Sensitive Hashing","Privacy-Preserving Distance Estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3F663B7E84B6E64A4B7335E787246316"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83278586/1703.07867.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of padova","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padova","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"d2298a1a-0cd6-4983-a20b-5e403cb3f4a0","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"christianipau","last":"Christiani","locid":"912427a9-6fae-4455-801a-5809fe371422","name":"Christiani, Tobias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","locid":"2b0f2ee4-24e0-4e0c-892e-2fa988f87110","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesco","key":"silvestripau","last":"Silvestri","name":"Silvestri, Francesco","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3196959.3196976","isbn":["9781450347068"],"pages":"89-104","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 37th ACM SIGMOD-SIGACT-SIGAI Symposium on Principles of Database System"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048008546"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ea56a443-a602-4cc9-88d5-b3544dabeac1","ku-c7995700-8fe0-4e70-9a2d-ded719bd3815"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Distance-Sensitive Hashing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.41-038407","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We present a data structure for *spherical range reporting* on a point set S, i.e., reporting all points in S that lie within radius r of a given query point q. Our solution builds upon the Locality-Sensitive Hashing (LSH) framework of Indyk and Motwani, which represents the asymptotically best solutions to near neighbor problems in high dimensions. While traditional LSH data structures have several parameters whose optimal values depend on the distance distribution from q to the points of S, our data structure is parameter-free, except for the space usage, which is configurable by the user. Nevertheless, its expected query time basically matches that of an LSH data structure whose parameters have been *optimally chosen for the data and query* in question under the given space constraints. In particular, our data structure provides a smooth trade-off between hard queries (typically addressed by standard LSH) and easy queries such as those where the number of points to report is a constant fraction of S, or where almost all points in S are far away from the query point. In contrast, known data structures fix LSH parameters based on certain parameters of the input alone. The algorithm has expected query time bounded by O(t(n/t)ρ), where t is the number of points to report and ρ∈(0,1) depends on the data distribution and the strength of the LSH family used. We further present a parameter-free way of using multi-probing, for LSH families that support it, and show that for many such families this approach allows us to get expected query time close to O(nρ+t), which is the best we can hope to achieve using LSH. The previously best running time in high dimensions was Ω(tnρ). For many data distributions where the intrinsic dimensionality of the point set close to q is low, we can give improved upper bounds on the expected query time.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ahle, Thomas Dybdahl","Pagh, Rasmus","Aumüller, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383612"],"event":{"acronym":"SODA","title":"ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["High dimensional data structures","Locality Sensitive Hashing LSH","Parameter free algorithms","Query optimization","Spherical range reporting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parameter free locality sensitive hashing for spherical range reporting","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1605.02673.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383612","identifier":[{"id":"85016199490","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a0d5fc29-0252-4510-bdb5-3ac2ceb0c76b"],"keyword":["- High-dimensional data structures","- Locality-Sensitive Hashing (LSH)","- Parameter-free algorithms","- Query optimization","- Spherical range reporting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CDA2F8C53873BE455518C50087E25F1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1605.02673.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82291122/1605.02673.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Dybdahl","key":"ahlepau","last":"Ahle","name":"Ahle, Thomas Dybdahl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"paghpau","last":"Pagh","name":"Pagh, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611974782.16","eisbn":["9781611974782"],"publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Twenty-Eighth Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85016199490"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a0d5fc29-0252-4510-bdb5-3ac2ceb0c76b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parameter-free Locality Sensitive Hashing for Spherical Range Reporting","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383612","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes ANN-Benchmarks, a tool for evaluating the performance of in-memory approximate nearest neighbor algorithms. It provides a standard interface for measuring the performance and quality achieved by nearest neighbor algorithms on different standard data sets. It supports several different ways of integrating k-NN algorithms, and its configuration system automatically tests a range of parameter settings for each algorithm. Algorithms are compared with respect to many different (approximate) quality measures, and adding more is easy and fast; the included plotting front-ends can visualise these as images, Open image in new window plots, and websites with interactive plots. ANN-Benchmarks aims to provide a constantly updated overview of the current state of the art of k-NN algorithms. In the short term, this overview allows users to choose the correct k-NN algorithm and parameters for their similarity search task; in the longer term, algorithm designers will be able to use this overview to test and refine automatic parameter tuning. The paper gives an overview of the system, evaluates the results of the benchmark, and points out directions for future work. Interestingly, very different approaches to k-NN search yield comparable quality-performance trade-offs. The system is available at http://sss.projects.itu.dk/ann-benchmarks/","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Bernhardsson, Erik","Faithfull, Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384166"],"event":{"acronym":"SISAP","title":"International Conference on Similarity Search and Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Parameter tuning","Performance evaluation","approximate nearest neighbor algorithms","k NN algorithm benchmarking","similarity search tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ann benchmarks a benchmarking tool for approximate nearest neighbor algorithms","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82351620/sisap2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384166","identifier":[{"id":"85031297593","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c59e669c-abd9-47e9-bc97-3ae2b692ad9e"],"keyword":["approximate nearest neighbor algorithms","k-NN algorithm benchmarking","parameter tuning","performance evaluation","similarity search tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-15B70B51B170F90EFD390A9CDBE30AF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82351620/sisap2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"bernhardssonpau","last":"Bernhardsson","name":"Bernhardsson, Erik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"faithfullpau","last":"Faithfull","name":"Faithfull, Alexander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-68474-1_3","eisbn":["9783319684741"],"isbn":["9783319684734"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"34-49","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"SISAP 2017: Similarity Search and Applications","title":"International Conference on Similarity Search and Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031297593"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c59e669c-abd9-47e9-bc97-3ae2b692ad9e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"ANN-Benchmarks: A Benchmarking Tool for Approximate Nearest Neighbor Algorithms","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384166","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We present an average case analysis of two variants of dual-pivot quicksort, one with a non-algorithmic comparison-optimal partitioning strategy, the other with a closely related algorithmic strategy. For both we calculate the expected number of comparisons exactly as well as asymptotically, in particular, we provide exact expressions for the linear, logarithmic, and constant terms. An essential step is the analysis of zeros of lattice paths in a certain probability model. Along the way a combinatorial identity is proven.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Dietzfelbinger, Martin","Heuberger, Clemens","Krenn, Daniel","Prodinger, Helmut"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384628"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-07","place":"Kraków, pl","start":"2016-07-04","title":"International Conference on Probabilistic, Combinatorial and Asymptotic Methods for the Analysis of Algorithms","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithmic strategy","Average case analysis","Comparison optimal partitioning","Dual pivot quicksort","Lattice paths analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"counting zeros in random walks on the integers and analysis of optimal dual pivot quicksort","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.04031v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384628","ids":["itu-e42c2005-9388-491e-b8dc-2188cd68a1ea"],"keyword":["Algorithmic strategy","Average case analysis","Comparison-optimal partitioning","Dual-pivot quicksort","Lattice paths analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FBDCB5846EF8BD610D1F579350F962EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.04031v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"dietzfelbingerpau","last":"Dietzfelbinger","name":"Dietzfelbinger, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Clemens","key":"heubergerpau","last":"Heuberger","name":"Heuberger, Clemens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"krennpau","last":"Krenn","name":"Krenn, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helmut","key":"prodingerpau","last":"Prodinger","name":"Prodinger, Helmut","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Jagiellonian University in Krakow","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 27th Conference on Probabilistic, Combinatorial and Asymptotic Methods for the Analysis of Algorithms"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e42c2005-9388-491e-b8dc-2188cd68a1ea"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Counting Zeros in Random Walks on the Integers and Analysis of Optimal Dual-Pivot Quicksort","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384628","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Multi-Pivot Quicksort refers to variants of classical quicksort where in the partitioning step k pivots are used to split the input into k + 1 segments. For many years, multi-pivot quicksort was regarded as impractical, but in 2009 a two-pivot approach by Yaroslavskiy, Bentley, and Bloch was chosen as the standard sorting algorithm in Sun’s Java 7. In 2014 at ALENEX, Kushagra et al. introduced an even faster algorithm that uses three pivots. This article studies what possible advantages multi-pivot quicksort might offer in general. The contributions are as follows: Natural comparison-optimal algorithms for multi-pivot quicksort are devised and analyzed. The analysis shows that the benefits of using multiple pivots with respect to the average comparison count are marginal and these strategies are inferior to simpler strategies such as the well-known median-of-k approach. A substantial part of the partitioning cost is caused by rearranging elements. A rigorous analysis of an algorithm for rearranging elements in the partitioning step is carried out, observing mainly how often array cells are accessed during partitioning. The algorithm behaves best if three to five pivots are used. Experiments show that this translates into good cache behavior and is closest to predicting observed running times of multi-pivot quicksort algorithms. Finally, it is studied how choosing pivots from a sample affects sorting cost. The study is theoretical in the sense that although the findings motivate design recommendations for multipivot quicksort algorithms that lead to running-time improvements over known algorithms in an experimental setting, these improvements are small.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aumüller, Martin","Dietzfelbinger, Martin","Klaue, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381544"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["3DInteractive","All Global Affiliations","Ilmenau University of Technology"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Multi Pivot","Quicksort","Sorting","Sorting and searching"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how good is multi pivot quicksort","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82372795/1510.04676.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381544","identifier":[{"id":"84992176837","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-12901260-9323-4782-865a-f4f0151d04a3"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Multi-Pivot","Quicksort","Sorting","Sorting and searching"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B02BBA58C54A3D4ED39EDA58073C3DEC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1510.04676.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82372795/1510.04676.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ilmenau university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ilmenau University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"3dinteractive","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"3DInteractive","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"aumüllerpau","last":"Aumüller","locid":"5f52759c-418a-41b7-bbdb-050492677284","name":"Aumüller, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-7212-6476","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"dietzfelbingerpau","last":"Dietzfelbinger","name":"Dietzfelbinger, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pascal","key":"klauepau","last":"Klaue","name":"Klaue, Pascal","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2963102","issn":["15496325","15496333"],"issn_org":["15496325"],"issue":"1","journal":"ACM Transactions on Algorithms","paperid":"8","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Algorithms","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84992176837"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-12901260-9323-4782-865a-f4f0151d04a3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Good Is Multi-Pivot Quicksort?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381544","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
